package ControlActivation {
    private import ScalarValues::*;
    requirement def SpecificSourceContracts {
        doc /* Each Scheme scope uses an evidence-bearing YuanxuContract whose value-contract delegates shape and normalization to concrete native Record and Function descriptors. Wire records are sealed, counters and credits are exact bounded integers, and Go and Rust independently validate the same artifact. Contract validity is required before registration and grants no execution authority. */
    }
    requirement def SourceStartupObservation {
        doc /* Local Go startup phases distinguish configuration readiness,
           authority connections/reconciliation and issuing Serve; only the
           actual authenticated channel proves readiness. Scheme compiler start,
           successful/failed reaping and artifact decoding are separate events.
           The native fixture records module readiness, entry, compilation and
           artifact write with SDK CPU/real clocks and host-wall microseconds.
           Clock origins differ; compare calibrated intervals and retain clock
           adjustment/profiling premises. Phase text is forgeable diagnostics,
           not proof of child quiescence, authority, source outcome or budget
           release. Preserve failed deadlines and distinguish unavailable process
           inventory from an absent process. No source/credential payload or path
           belongs in producer-created phase attributes. */
    }
    requirement def GovernorSourceHandoff {
        doc /* The Rust host snapshots the independently admitted original
           artifact before producer invocation. Candidate consistency alone
           cannot authorize changed family, body/profile commitments or budget.
           Complete native record equality yields BoundSource data only. The
           host must not derive its expectation from the returned candidate.
           Callback provenance and current source/history/Policy/fence/CAS
           remain separate. Local binding burns no durable authority. */
        doc /* Go preparation discovers the selected SDK home from explicit
           environment or the selected compiler, refusing an invalid explicit
           home. Embedded module lookup cannot infer it from the Rust executable.
           The prepared check-scheme owner qualifies the fixed SDK graph after
           standard Gerbil tests. Runtime Rust/Arrow checks enable converter
           features without linking this qualification graph. Source contracts
           preserve field-symbol versus identifier-string key kinds in both
           directions; file JSON/YAML decoding stays in Go. */
        doc /* The Gateway scope exposes typed call-scoped capture returning
           an inert GatewayArtifact Record. A serialized sink accepts exactly one emission,
           latches caught duplicate attempts, requires true producer completion
           and closes on return or exception. Old inherited sinks cannot emit
           into a new capture. Both file and memory facades reuse actual admitted
           AA/Governor/Cedar production and currentness checks; the emitter's
           Boolean result is distinct from an admission evidence object. The native SDK strong root is converted into concrete Rust-owned data before any await; no JSON blob is the in-process carrier. Host/export authentication and final authority remain separate. */
        doc /* Cross-language qualification imports the package-built Scheme
           fixture library. Standard gerbil build owns its expansion; the fixture
           is not a production module or executable. Changing load ownership
           neither changes Governance semantics nor proves a timeout root cause.
           Native properties and actual publication/send controls remain required. */
        doc /* Scheme captures independent canonical bytes for original Profile
           identity/revision/owner, model identity, complete native threat data
           and assessment context before invoking an AA method. A callback may
           not change these data or replace the selected method references and
           then validate two agreeing live aliases. Original blocking threats
           refuse before callback execution. These local snapshots supply no
           producer authentication, durable source cut, general closure purity
           or final-send authority. Existing Policy projection and Rust current
           execution checks remain separate. */
        doc /* Scheme projects native governor open-patterns after denylist, conflict and max-actionable clipping. Selected nodes, original task nodes and plan nodes must form the same duplicate-free set. A typed inert Governance assessment must match the exact task/plan/publication source serialized with recursively sorted object keys while preserving array order and exact integers, Profile identity/revision/owner, threat-model identity and complete assessed threats. Native blocking threats cannot be erased by a ready flag. False Policy preflight or Governance results reject. Assessment is a trusted compilation fact, never a portable execution permit. Candidate actionable-patterns are not a qualified handoff or a monetary reservation. */
    }
    requirement def PolicyCAbiIsInert {
        doc /* One Scheme source-bytes owner rejects empty/overlong character
           inputs before UTF-8 allocation and then checks the encoded byte bound
           for each Policy/schema value. Native Record predicates and actual C
           FFI reuse it; Rust independently checks both borrowed lengths and UTF-8.
           Size acceptance never supplies current authority or a send permit. */
        doc /* Synchronous Gambit C FFI borrows bounded immutable UTF-8 data for Rust typed Cedar validation. No returned status, buffer, callback or source artifact is an execution capability. Rust final publication and execution repeat authoritative checks. */
    }
    requirement def GovernancePolicyProjection {
        doc /* Borrowed validation retains pinned Tokio request/answer channels
           and the existing async admission task. Custom Condvar and ready-permit
           dispatch candidates were tested and rejected without attributable
           benefit on the contended Host. Keep callback on the polling caller;
           never offload borrowed state or extend its lifetime unsafely. Drop
           before answer refuses; queued true survives caller drop; accepted
           work owns its original lease through native completion. There is no
           spin loop, cached authority or early unknown-budget release. Future
           ready-permit review must preserve registered semaphore fairness and
           distinguish admission from durable authority CAS ordering. Retain
           frozen baseline/candidate binaries, all ABBA and native-control
           samples at actual CPUs with minimum four, Host-load observations and
           borrowed-guard/cancellation/panic/recovery evidence. Neither fewer
           source-level hops nor local correctness establishes throughput gain. */
        doc /* Hot-path attribution uses test-only clocks at the existing public
           provider seam and borrowed validator. Separate original-home lock
           wait, API duration, provider pre-body/body/post-body, physical gets/
           puts, validator read+integrity/decode and residual rendezvous time.
           ProfilePort runs the borrowed validator on the async caller through
           request/answer channels while the native worker holds its transaction;
           body residual is not pure engine CPU. FULL post-body latency includes
           COMMIT and release, not isolated fsync. Do not replace the provider or
           weaken durability for instrumentation. Retain per-request samples,
           rotated controls and cancellation/recovery tests at actual Host CPUs.
           Host jitter requires corroboration; missing kernel I/O evidence must
           remain explicit. Existing SPEC semantics and final-use ownership stay. */
        doc /* A sequential diagnostic may invoke the existing public metadata
           engine with the same immutable body, authority vector and native store
           while a CPU-sized runtime services driver I/O. It removes ProfilePort
           admission/rendezvous only as a causal control, never as a production
           replacement for borrowed guards, cancellation or final admission.
           Distinguish this lower-layer control from full-path throughput. */
        doc /* CPU-matched writer requalification uses max(4, available Host CPUs)
           for runtime, write/shared workers and reusable capacity in the native
           lifecycle target and real-content paired benchmark. Record actual
           CPUs, workers and blocking capacity. Compare WAL, fresh MVCC and reuse
           in rotated matching rounds for original hot and independent homes;
           retain every sample, refusal and Unknown. Do not overlap this task's
           builds/tests with measurement or infer a new performance gain from
           historical runs. Preserve the 30-second bound, exact operation and
           authority recovery, held unknown exposure and terminal old owners.
           Provider reconstruction and process-death evidence stay distinct. */
        doc /* Native multithreaded acceptance uses at least four Tokio workers;
           explicit blocking-thread budgets also have a four-thread minimum. CPU-derived performance drivers
           scale to the available Host CPUs with a four-worker minimum and report
           actual CPU/worker counts separately. Logical one-slot refusal controls
           are resource-bound tests, never a reduction of runtime thread count.
           Earlier two-thread receipts remain historical, not current acceptance. */
        doc /* A SQL writer owner becomes terminal when close starts. Recovery
           constructs a fresh provider around the original durable store; the
           stopped object cannot reopen or accept a late lease. Open/close hold
           one lifecycle lock across pool, reader and bootstrap resource changes.
           Cancellation is not rollback, close is not domain revocation, and a
           free slot is not discharged exposure. Driver Unknown discards a writer;
           lost delivery after known commit may leave a healthy physical session
           but still requires exact original operation/authority recovery. No
           resource transition grants semantic authority or permits refund. */
        doc /* Reusable Turso writers are bounded exclusive execution resources,
           never cached authority or send capabilities. FULL is configured and
           verified on private connection creation. Only successful COMMIT plus
           confirmed autocommit permits return to the idle set; driver error/Unknown,
           failed cleanup or unwinding discards the connection. Active plus idle
           writers cannot exceed the explicit Host capacity. Close stops new
           leases, refuses outstanding work and discards idle sessions; recovery
           uses a new provider and cannot inherit a prior lease. Existing home-sequence, original keys,
           unknown obligations and final Rust admission remain unchanged. */
        doc /* Turso concurrent admission is an explicit storage execution mode.
           The existing canonical home-sequence is the common write-conflict
           witness for content, authority changes and outbox acknowledgment.
           Independent homes may execute concurrently; shared claims and budget
           remain in their original canonical home. No namespace sharding may
           evade that witness. A validation callback runs at most once per
           attempt, without external effects. COMMIT failure stays Unknown and
           recovery queries the original operation; no implicit retry or ticket
           recreation is permitted. FULL durability, bounded Host workers and
           drain-before-close remain required. Existing stores cannot silently
           switch journal modes. SPEC semantics and Quint timing ownership do
           not move into the storage provider. */
        doc /* MRR Data owns the optional Turso storage adapter. Weaver supplies
           the original canonical coordination home and immutable obligation body;
           reconnects cannot choose a new home. Content durability precedes the
           metadata decision. Metadata without a recoverable body denies readiness
           and retains unknown exposure. Validation callbacks are inert, and exact
           replay or outbox acknowledgment creates no live send capability.
           Final Rust admission rechecks the current retained cut, owner/fence,
           Policy and existing one-use ticket after any storage approval. Generic
           backend receipt equality does not prove this final-use refinement. */
        doc /* Replay revision admission reads the immutable captured parent from
           the existing review requirement, not candidate metadata. Full original
           predecessor bytes match that authority-owned Policy/schema commitment;
           both selected PolicySets match the actual fixed SPEC manifest. Missing
           predecessor, legacy absent schema or a different schema rejects this
           replay profile without clearing pending intent. Heavy replay occurs
           outside SQL; registration and final CAS retain current-parent checks.
           Historical exact replay remains observation and supplies no no-gain,
           source authentication, independent root or provider-send authority. */
        doc /* Source RPC identity derives from actual authenticated mTLS leaf,
           SPKI and role-credential bytes. The existing ledger enrolls an empty
           unowned store once, retains the key prefix and decides exact handoffs.
           Every source mutation rechecks current identity under its final SQL
           transaction; startup pin restore cannot lower that local authority.
           Historical handoff receipts grant no new permission. Source SPKI
           continuity is not independent subject/incarnation issuance, full
           reviewed-publication qualification or whole-store anti-rollback. */
        doc /* The retained recovery cut includes the four existing domain
           prefixes, execution owner/epoch, monotone one-use burns and the original
           reservation/unknown-exposure commitment. The admission transaction
           retains the burn and full obligation body together before any callback.
           A missing reply cannot split these into independently reusable rights.
           Root generation and qualified observations change with that cut. */
        doc /* Local exposure/burn projections must conform to the retained cut
           both when qualifying recovery and at actual admission. A restored zero
           hold or missing receipt denies readiness; it does not establish unused
           funds. Rebuilding records cannot recreate a lost live send ticket.
           Final use still requires the existing Rust owner/fence/current-Policy
           checks. Settlement requires its existing SPEC/domain witnesses and is
           not decided by the temporal recovery envelope. */
        doc /* An independent retained-root witness binds the authority namespace,
           authenticated generation and inherited full-content source prefix.
           Configuration cannot enroll a replacement root. Registration and final
           publication join that witness; lost confirmation is reconciled by the
           original immutable decision, never by adopting a restored local root.
           Retention confirmation is an existing-authority commit witness, not an
           assertion that writes to two independent stores are atomic. */
        doc /* Root retention coverage must include affine transport burns and
           original claim/reservation/account/history state, not only the source
           registry or four prefix ordinals. Equal prefixes can coexist with a
           rolled-back burned table. A local held=0 after restore is not a release
           certificate. Missing domain bodies or exposure projections deny
           activation and preserve the original unknown obligation. Same-root
           failover must inherit this complete recovery image before requalifying;
           old worker handles and historical receipts confer no current rights. */
        doc /* Registry recovery has distinct reconstruction, qualification and
           final-use steps. Qualification binds the complete inherited prefix to
           the current authority identity/generation, source cut and observer
           context. Row equality or a persisted recovered flag is insufficient.
           Restart, handoff, revocation, prefix append or projection loss requires
           revalidation; final CAS rechecks both qualification and current data.
           A stale NotFound is not permission to replace the original artifact,
           resolve pending or release unknown budget. Qualification is never a
           transport permit and cannot repair rollback of its own trust root. */
        doc /* verify_publication_replay delegates to the actual fixed SPEC
           ValidatedManifest/SchemaBoundReceipt runtime. The candidate's complete
           policy ID/body set and schema must equal the original publication.
           register_replay_checked_review validates before registration, then the
           deciding transaction rechecks the captured parent and original pending.
           Failed replay leaves the original unresolved. Native replay is finite
           evidence; actual no-gain, producer authenticity, semantic parent/Profile
           qualification and independent registry recovery are separate obligations.
           Cedar source may use official materialized PolicySet JSON to preserve
           named IDs; renderer comments cannot substitute for those identities. */
        doc /* Recovery joins one independently retained authority generation and
           committed prefix, not a maximum epoch copied from startup config.
           Epoch/owner, issuance/revocation decisions, original artifact bindings
           and publication outcomes inherit that prefix together. A new leader
           may activate only after proving prefix inheritance; an unavailable or
           ambiguous authority keeps registration and publication disabled. */
        doc /* A process restart invalidates observer read capabilities even
           when the authority epoch is unchanged. Late reads and acknowledgments
           are historical observations; they cannot activate a new observer or
           replace a fresh final join. Recovery distinguishes an exact committed
           registration from a missing local projection. Unknown is neither an
           abort nor permission to register replacement evidence. */
        doc /* Trust anchors and prefix retention belong to the independent
           authority deployment contract; a shared Kubernetes identity, restored
           startup certificate or ordinary SQLite restart supplies neither.
           Consistent rollback of the entire local registry can erase an earlier
           artifact binding. Keep its executable counterexample until an actual
           independent authority adapter demonstrates recovery. Runtime assets
           obey Project.ProductionAssetBoundary; live authority state belongs to
           configured durable storage, never a promoted prod config value. */
        doc /* The existing Rust ledger now supplies a trusted-host local review
           admission primitive. stage_reviewed_authority atomically latches its
           exact command and authority-selected complete Policy/schema parent.
           register_approved_review retains full immutable upstream evidence.
           Final publication rechecks this binding under the deciding transaction;
           ordinary staging cannot downgrade the requirement. Missing review keeps
           an eligible proposal pending; a stale parent CAS records only its own
           rejection. Native host authentication, actual Delta qualification,
           independent registry prefix recovery and RPC integration remain open.
           No source credential or opaque artifact is promoted to semantic proof. */
        doc /* Final source-use admission joins the authority-owned epoch,
           revocation and issuance prefix, artifact registry and publication
           parent/fence. Restored configuration or cached observations cannot
           lower this floor. A registry append between read and CAS requires a
           fresh join. Unavailable authority retains pending and unknown holds;
           an absent response never establishes abort or permits cached fallback. */
        doc /* Source-role authentication is bootstrap input. A current registrar
           binding independently fixes subject, incarnation, public key, scope,
           audience, epoch and credential identity. Possession covers the exact
           operation transcript; register and publish have separate purposes.
           Revocation and final use serialize at the authority journal. A delayed
           issuer outcome remains historical and cannot activate an old epoch. */
        doc /* The historical startup-pin rollback counterexample is now a
           native regression: after an explicit durable key handoff, restoring
           its old transport pin still cannot authorize source writes. Retain
           whole-store rollback and missing incarnation/independent authority
           counterexamples; the local key floor does not close those premises. */
        doc /* Delta registration linearizes at the existing independent commit
           authority, not at a local projection write or an RPC reply. Its exact
           original command/artifact registration is immutable and survives owner
           handoff. Local projection rollback is repaired from that authority;
           a missing projection blocks final CAS and is not an artifact rejection. */
        doc /* Final publication must join the authority registry prefix and
           authenticated registrar incarnation/term in the same authoritative
           decision. Independent precheck followed by local SQLite commit is
           insufficient. Source-role TLS/token authorization does not establish
           registrar incarnation. Current production accepts retained source-role
           credentials after restart; keep that expected coverage counterexample. */
        doc /* Publication pending admission is command-specific: a final CAS
           may resolve its own staged intent while administrative siblings remain.
           Requiring globally empty pending here deadlocks progress. Provider
           effects still require the distinct global resolved-pending barrier. */
        doc /* Publication review binds the independent authoritative parent,
           exact original command, approved Delta/replay artifact and deciding
           source cut under one final CAS. Caller-selected parent/evidence and
           cached prechecks are insufficient. SPEC PublicationReview composes
           LeanPoo Contract.bindEvidence with generic ZeroTrust requirements;
           Weaver's existing recovery Step supplies outcome/intent/accounting
           preservation under an explicit native refinement premise. */
        doc /* Review registration is immutable per original command ID.
           Unknown registration or publication replies retain pending intent.
           Replacement evidence rejects; stale parent/fence is an original
           terminal rejection, never an implicit rebase. Resolving one proposal
           preserves siblings. Historical outcomes remain queryable but confer
           no current execution authority. Production RPC has no Delta artifact
           field yet: command commitment tests do not qualify review admission. */
        doc /* Native Cedar Policy values and cedar-language GovernanceSource assets project to one exact ordered Cedar policy set. Assets use explicit confined roots and bounded regular-file reads. Unsupported domain obligations reject. The publication carries the exact projected bytes; the native source manifest is compilation evidence and not a runtime permit. */
        doc /* Reviewed no-gain publication additionally needs exact original
           parent/profile/source/schema/policy evidence bound at the final CAS.
           Typed validation, a source credential and a publication receipt do
           not establish Authorization Delta review. Current Rust publication
           accepts an authorized widening command without such an artifact;
           preserve that expected counterexample as an unimplemented target. */
    }
    requirement def ControlActivationAcknowledgment {
        doc /* Go exposes operation ingress only after original-task registration and an exact committed publication acknowledgment. Unknown outcomes cannot activate or trigger automatic rebase. Exact recovery may observe a historical decision without making it current authority. */
        doc /* Before a new final publication, Go stages its exact original ID,
           parent, fence and Policy/schema body at the Rust source owner before
           task registration. Each staged task atomically binds its immutable
           family to its original publication key. A stage
           key proves durable pending or an already recorded exact decision,
           never current authority. All effect guards reject any unresolved
           Policy proposal under the same SQLite transaction. Final publication
           records committed/rejected outcome and removes only that proposal
           atomically. Lost replies and restart preserve pending and unknown
           holds. This administrative Policy proposal protocol is not the
           external hard-fact capture/projection or independent floor protocol. */
        doc /* Go readiness is not the Rust operation-role authorization boundary.
           A materialized task whose original publication is missing or rejected
           must not execute under another current allowing image. Every effect
           guard requires that task's exact committed origin plus current Cedar,
           pending, claim, budget and fence checks. Direct trusted registration
           replay cannot erase an existing origin; later Policy updates preserve
           a committed original assignment. */
    }
    requirement def ControlStreamRecoveryBinding {
        doc /* Go compiles proposals against the frozen original task and forwards one Rust execution stream over mutual TLS gRPC. Source methods are absent from operation ingress. Shared budgets, original claims and unknown holds survive partial output, revocation, SDK retries and both process restarts. Previously authorized queue entries may drain after revocation. */
    }
    part def SchemeAuthor {
        attribute governorOpenSelection : Boolean;
        attribute inertPolicyValidation : Boolean;
    }
    part def GoControl {
        attribute acknowledgedPublication : Boolean;
        attribute active : Boolean;
    }
    part def RustAuthority {
        attribute mandatoryLocalReview : Boolean;
        attribute originalReviewRegistered : Boolean;
        attribute unresolvedPolicyProposals : Integer;
        attribute originalTaskPublicationCommitted : Boolean;
        attribute currentRevision : Integer;
        attribute consumed : Boolean;
        attribute heldBudget : Integer;
    }
}
